# This project is deployed to Ubuntu and its shell scripts are executed there.
# A carriage return at the end of a `set -o pipefail` line becomes
# `set: pipefail: invalid option name` AT RUN TIME on the target host, and
# `bash -n` does not catch it - it is a valid script containing an option name
# that happens to end in a control character.
#
# Every tracked file here is stored with LF today, measured with
# `git ls-files --eol` against the INDEX rather than by reading a working tree
# (a Windows clone with core.autocrlf=true shows CRLF for everything and says
# nothing about what is committed). This file keeps it that way after the next
# edit on a Windows box, and the release pipeline refuses a committed CR on
# every tag either way.
* text=auto eol=lf

*.sh   text eol=lf
*.bash text eol=lf
*.py   text eol=lf
*.csv  text eol=lf
*.md   text eol=lf
*.yml  text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf

*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.ico  binary
*.docx binary
*.pdf  binary
